# Scrum Poker — environment variables
#
# All variables are optional. With none set, the app uses STUN-only ICE
# (Google + Twilio public servers). Peers behind symmetric NAT, corporate
# firewalls blocking UDP, or browsers with aggressive WebRTC privacy
# settings (Arc, Brave) may then fail to connect.
#
# To improve coverage, configure ONE OR BOTH TURN providers below. Both
# providers can run in parallel — ICE will pick whichever relay candidate
# succeeds first.
#
# Vite injects these at build time, so deployments must set them as
# secrets in the build environment (e.g. GitHub Actions repo secrets).
# Local dev: copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values.

# ─── Open Relay (Metered.ca) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free tier: 20 GB / month, no credit card. Static credentials are
# intentionally PUBLIC — Metered publishes them as a free service for OSS
# projects, so it's safe to ship them in the client bundle.
# Sign up & retrieve credentials: https://www.metered.ca/tools/openrelay/
# VITE_TURN_OPENRELAY_URLS=turn:openrelay.metered.ca:80,turn:openrelay.metered.ca:443?transport=tcp,turns:openrelay.metered.ca:443
# VITE_TURN_OPENRELAY_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_OPENRELAY_CREDENTIAL=

# ─── Cloudflare TURN (via Worker) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Free tier: 1,000 GB / month (shared with Realtime SFU). Anycast multi-region.
# REQUIRES a credit card on Cloudflare (you won't be charged at this scale,
# but the card is mandatory).
#
# Security: NEVER ship Cloudflare's TURN_KEY_ID / TURN_KEY_API_TOKEN in the
# client bundle. Anyone with the key can mint relay credentials and drain
# your free quota. The supported pattern is to deploy the small Worker at
# `infra/turn-token-worker/` and put its public URL here. The Worker
# fetches short-lived (4 h) credentials from Cloudflare on demand.
#
# Worker setup:
#   cd infra/turn-token-worker
#   wrangler secret put TURN_KEY_ID
#   wrangler secret put TURN_KEY_API_TOKEN
#   wrangler deploy
# VITE_TURN_CF_TOKEN_URL=https://scrum-poker-turn.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev

# ─── Debug: WebRTC stats poller ────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set to '1', peerManager dumps `getStats()` selected-pair info
# (iceState, candidateType, bytesSent, bytesReceived, RTT) to console.debug
# every 10 s while in a room. Useful for diagnosing relay vs direct,
# bandwidth, or sluggish networks. Production builds tree-shake this out
# when the variable is unset.
# VITE_DEBUG_WEBRTC=1
